1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 1]
He knows that name very well. The man dismissed as uncontrollable, a swordmaster locked in his room, a man out of his mind, is Count Perdium's useless oldest son: Ghislain Perdium, slumped alone in a wrecked room.

2
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 2]
A bloodied knight who calls himself the best knight of the North cannot believe he was defeated by that garbage human being. The hooded victor tells him the trap was warm and cozy, and he paid a lot to build it.

3
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 3]
The hooded figure asks, "Do you like it?" The knight finally recognises him. "Y-you're that garbage, Ghislain...?" he demands how Ghislain knew his plans. Ghislain advances through the fallen soldiers. "Not just that."

4
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 4]
He knew how many of them there were, who the spies were, and who sent their reinforcements. "I knew it all from the start."

5
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 5]
The defeated knight looks tiny, cradled in a giant armoured hand. He cannot believe it. He has always been a hidden ace card, he insists, and this could not have happened.

6
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 6]
He curses Ghislain as a useless piece of shit, and is cut off mid-insult. "Shut it." Ghislain stands over his fallen foe and warns him to invade as many times as he wants, because he will win the war every time. "It's because I've got all the plans."

7
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 7]
A year ago, in a military camp in the Luthania Kingdom near the Perdium estate, Ghislain wakes in a panic. "Wh-what just happened?" he gasps, staring at his own hands. "I'm alive?" His eyes widen: just a while ago, he was—

8
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 8]
A blinding flash cuts him off, and the memory returns. His great sword spins away and falls, a blade finds its mark, and the bloodied Ghislain is cut down. Idun, one of the continent's top seven, the Noble Knight, stands over him. "The war is over."

9
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 9]
Idun asks for any last words. Ghislain has none, only his unfulfilled revenge. Dying, he snarls, "Die, you sickening bastard!" Idun sneers, "How arrogant." Then he reveals that the Mercenary King was the oldest son of the fallen Perdium household, who left after his sister died.

10
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 10]
Ghislain demands how a man from a different kingdom could know that. Idun says of course he knows, because he worked hard long ago to track Ghislain down. His side worked with the Delphine household to bring down Ghislain's family. Ghislain reels at one word. "We"?!

11
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 11]
Others were behind his family's fall besides Duke Delphine's household. Idun refuses to explain further. Ghislain will be dead soon, so he should just accept his fate. Ghislain screams, "You bastard! I will never forgive you!!!" Idun answers, "Okay."

12
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 12]
At that moment, Idun decapitates him. Yet here Ghislain is, with his head still on his shoulders. Was it all a hallucination? He is in his younger body too.

13
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 13]
Was he taken captive and used as a lab rat for the mages? He vows to make them regret keeping him alive. Then a voice calls out, "Young Master!" Perdium's soldier Ricardo enters and urges him out.

14
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 14]
Ghislain silences Ricardo with a sword to his throat. "Sh. I'll let you live if you answer my questions," he threatens, "or maybe not." Ricardo stammers in shock, protesting that this is crossing the line. Ghislain is baffled. Ricardo is the one being threatened.

15
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 15]
Ricardo snaps back. Ghislain only tired himself out from a tantrum earlier and fell asleep, throwing a tantrum about commanding the group to raid the orcs. "What? I threw a tantrum?!" Ricardo tells him to get his stuff together. People are waiting.

16
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 16]
"My stuff...? Where are we going?" Ghislain asks. "To the Perdium estate, of course," Ricardo answers. Ghislain freezes and grabs Ricardo. "Say that again!" "P-Perdium... you mean the fallen Perdium estate?"

17
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 17]
It really is the Perdium estate, yet he saw it reduced to ashes back then. Ricardo whispers that he must have had a terrible nightmare; the Count would kick him out for calling his household fallen. Ghislain pinches his cheek. "Am I dreaming?" The pain tells him no.

18
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 18]
A younger face, and the estate in its original state. That means only one thing. Standing before a giant clock, Ghislain asks, "I traveled back to the past?"

19
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 19]
His younger self resented the household. Feeling inferior, he caused trouble, and the household avoided him. Unable to stand the criticism, he ran away from home. Several years later, he became a mercenary, surviving countless battles. He returned to atone, but his household had already been crushed to dust.

20
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 20]
"I lost everything," he remembers, but now the intact banner is still all here. All the people he holds dear are still here. He can hardly believe it. He wants to sing in joy. But it is too early to rejoice.

21
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 21]
Ricardo said they were here to raid the orcs. Ghislain cannot forget that day: this is the day most people in the raid squad will die. In his past life, he followed the raid squad to make a name for himself. The report said three orcs, but there were more than twenty, and almost everyone died because he insisted on commanding the squad.

22
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 22]
It should be doable, he thinks, since those orcs did not really have a strategy. The problem is whether the men will trust him, when they all think he is some useless bastard.

23
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 23]
Debris from a shattered structure flies through the camp as Ghislain turns toward the crash. The wreckage slams into the ground. The soldiers panic. "It's the orcs!!!" The orcs charge into the camp, weapons raised,

24
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 24]
Ghislain is stunned. "Already? Did they get here this fast in my past life too?!" The orcs tear through the camp, hurling soldiers aside. A voice roars, "Get into formation!"

25
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 25]
Raid Squad Commander Skovan charges in, shouting, "Do not panic. Get into defense formation!" An orc's sweeping blow sends soldiers flying as Skovan is knocked back. They were ambushed unprepared, and there are far more orcs than reported. At this rate, they will all die.

26
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 26]
"Behind you!!!" A huge orc raises its axe over Skovan. A desperate slash meets the orc's attack as the fight turns chaotic. Ghislain rushes past Skovan toward the orc, sword ready.

27
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 27]
Skovan stares in disbelief. "Huh?" Then, "Young Master...?" Ghislain cuts the orc down. The orc catches his blade bare-handed, but Ghislain slashes through its arm and drives his blade onward.

28
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 28]
Skovan and the soldiers stare, stunned. The wounded orc roars in pain. Ghislain stands over the fallen orc, sword in hand, He cannot use mana in this younger body, and wishes he had returned to the past earlier.

29
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 29]
He turns to the fallen Skovan. "You're the commander, right?" Skovan stammers, "Y-Young Master?" Ghislain holds out his hand. "Give it." Skovan is baffled. "Sorry?" "The commander rights."
